[DESCRIPTION]: The function `f(x)` takes a numerical input and returns the complement of the input value incremented by 1 for negative inputs and decremented by 1 for positive inputs.

[DOMAIN]: The domain of the function is all real numbers, and there is no interval where the function displays unexpected behavior.

[CODE]: Here is the Python code that approximates the behavior of the function:

